1
00:00:03,802 --> 00:00:04,720
[grunts]

2
00:00:04,803 --> 00:00:07,723
Geez, he's better than last time.

3
00:00:07,806 --> 00:00:09,599
Not to mention he's beefed up, too.

4
00:00:09,683 --> 00:00:11,977
And yet, he still seems
to be faster than before.

5
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:15,147
[student 1] Even our second-years
don't stand a chance against him.

6
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,358
[both] Thank you for the match.

7
00:00:21,445 --> 00:00:24,114
You're really tearing it up
out there, Yusa.

8
00:00:24,197 --> 00:00:25,615
But this match just now,

9
00:00:25,699 --> 00:00:28,118
you could've stopped
five more of his points.

10
00:00:28,201 --> 00:00:30,412
In the second half, you used a cut,
but let me tell you,

11
00:00:30,495 --> 00:00:32,748
if it were me, I would've
smashed it right back at him.

12
00:00:32,831 --> 00:00:34,750
- [snoring]
- No naps!

13
00:00:35,959 --> 00:00:39,254
I don't have any free time
to talk to you right now, Yakushiji.

14
00:00:39,337 --> 00:00:41,798
If you have time to sleep,
you have time to talk.

15
00:00:41,882 --> 00:00:44,092
Can't you see? I'm clearly taking a break.

16
00:00:45,093 --> 00:00:47,596
I wanna be ready
to go up against that guy,

17
00:00:47,679 --> 00:00:49,765
so I need to make sure I'm in good shape.

18
00:00:49,848 --> 00:00:52,017
[Yakushiji] Oh, Haryu?

19
00:00:52,601 --> 00:00:55,687
Well, everybody knows he's
Eimei's best badminton player.

20
00:00:55,771 --> 00:00:58,774
And not that we like to bring it up,
but he made it to nationals.

21
00:00:58,857 --> 00:01:02,444
He always manages to aim
for the toughest spots on the court,

22
00:01:02,527 --> 00:01:03,779
so it's pretty fun.

23
00:01:03,862 --> 00:01:06,239
Huh? That ain't fun, kid!

24
00:01:06,323 --> 00:01:07,532
Really?

25
00:01:07,616 --> 00:01:10,827
Yusa! Sorry it's back-to-back,
but you're up.

26
00:01:11,328 --> 00:01:12,287
Against who?

27
00:01:12,954 --> 00:01:14,331
They said it's Inomata.

28
00:01:14,414 --> 00:01:15,916
He's a first-year like you.

29
00:01:15,999 --> 00:01:17,125
Inomata?

30
00:01:18,752 --> 00:01:19,920
Ready to play.

31
00:01:21,421 --> 00:01:22,714
[Yusa] Oh.

32
00:01:22,798 --> 00:01:25,801
It's the guy who told me
where the gym was earlier.

33
00:01:27,803 --> 00:01:29,805
[opening theme song playing]

34
00:01:54,204 --> 00:01:57,624
BLUE BOX

35
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:01,229
{\an8}EPISODE 18
I KNOW

36
00:03:03,565 --> 00:03:05,525
[upbeat instrumental music playing]

37
00:03:15,327 --> 00:03:16,953
[Taiki] Let's go!

38
00:03:18,079 --> 00:03:19,039
Huh.

39
00:03:21,374 --> 00:03:22,751
Let's have a good match!

40
00:03:23,752 --> 00:03:25,003
Yeah, good luck.

41
00:03:25,086 --> 00:03:27,297
Hey! It's Inomata's turn!

42
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,132
Looks like the match is about to start.

43
00:03:30,717 --> 00:03:32,135
Girl, what are you doing?

44
00:03:32,219 --> 00:03:35,138
Didn't you promise him
you'd be there to cheer him on?

45
00:03:35,847 --> 00:03:38,016
Yeah, I said that I would come watch.

46
00:03:38,099 --> 00:03:39,935
I didn't promise any cheering.

47
00:03:40,018 --> 00:03:41,394
It's the same thing.

48
00:03:41,478 --> 00:03:46,274
Isn't this a revenge match against the guy
he lost to at prefectural qualifiers?

49
00:03:46,358 --> 00:03:47,400
Yeah, it is.

50
00:03:48,985 --> 00:03:50,570
Look, I know that, but...

51
00:03:55,659 --> 00:03:57,911
I don't wanna see him how he was that day.

52
00:03:57,994 --> 00:03:59,955
I didn't have any idea

53
00:04:00,038 --> 00:04:02,791
of what I could
possibly say to him then, either.

54
00:04:03,917 --> 00:04:06,127
Why are you assuming
he's gonna lose this time, though?

55
00:04:06,211 --> 00:04:08,797
[exclaims] That is not
what I'm trying to say!

56
00:04:10,257 --> 00:04:11,800
- Oh, it started!
- [Hina gasps softly]

57
00:04:13,176 --> 00:04:17,097
Look, Hina, I don't think you need to
worry about what you're gonna say to him.

58
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:20,558
I do think you should get up and watch
the match with me for your own sake.

59
00:04:21,268 --> 00:04:23,353
Oh. He's rallying well.

60
00:04:31,903 --> 00:04:33,697
- [grunts]
- [gasps]

61
00:04:34,489 --> 00:04:36,700
[gasps]

62
00:04:40,036 --> 00:04:42,038
[Nagisa] Everybody's playing pretty well.

63
00:04:42,122 --> 00:04:45,208
[Chinatsu] They're supposed to be
the best school in our prefecture.

64
00:04:46,418 --> 00:04:48,586
Oh. He just scored!

65
00:04:48,670 --> 00:04:50,630
Wait, which court are you looking at?

66
00:04:50,714 --> 00:04:52,841
It's second from the left in the back.

67
00:04:52,924 --> 00:04:54,092
All right, let's see.

68
00:04:55,176 --> 00:04:57,095
[grunts] Yes!

69
00:04:58,263 --> 00:05:02,058
Uh... Chii, so if I've got this wrong,
I apologize...

70
00:05:02,142 --> 00:05:03,059
[Chinatsu] Hm?

71
00:05:03,810 --> 00:05:05,979
Then again, maybe I shouldn't...

72
00:05:06,062 --> 00:05:07,147
Spit it out.

73
00:05:08,106 --> 00:05:09,107
By any chance,

74
00:05:09,190 --> 00:05:11,359
when I called you on your birthday,

75
00:05:11,443 --> 00:05:13,111
were you together with that guy?

76
00:05:13,194 --> 00:05:14,362
[Chinatsu exclaims]

77
00:05:14,446 --> 00:05:15,613
Before I hung up,

78
00:05:15,697 --> 00:05:18,199
<i>I heard another voice for a second.</i>

79
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:21,119
So does that mean
the two of you are dating?

80
00:05:21,202 --> 00:05:23,371
Just tell me, come on! I am your friend!

81
00:05:23,455 --> 00:05:25,081
You may be in the same gym,

82
00:05:25,165 --> 00:05:27,751
but you don't have
to get all shy about it!

83
00:05:27,834 --> 00:05:28,877
[Chinatsu sighs]

84
00:05:29,878 --> 00:05:31,212
It's not like that.

85
00:05:33,631 --> 00:05:36,426
You know how a family's
been letting me live with them?

86
00:05:37,093 --> 00:05:38,511
That family's Taiki's.

87
00:05:38,595 --> 00:05:39,512
Huh?

88
00:05:41,181 --> 00:05:43,349
Both of our moms know each other.

89
00:05:43,433 --> 00:05:46,770
And they happened to have
a spare room open, so I--

90
00:05:46,853 --> 00:05:47,687
GRAB

91
00:05:47,771 --> 00:05:51,274
- Huh?
- Are you a freakin' idiot?

92
00:05:51,357 --> 00:05:54,652
I am super pumped
that you decided to stay in Japan.

93
00:05:54,736 --> 00:05:57,155
But living with a boy
when we're all dating-age?

94
00:05:57,238 --> 00:06:00,408
You just don't do it!
Tell me, what if something happens?

95
00:06:00,492 --> 00:06:03,328
Don't you know that saying,
"all men are beasts"?

96
00:06:03,411 --> 00:06:05,205
Like, you know what
my little brother does?

97
00:06:05,288 --> 00:06:08,416
His... [elephant roars]
goes... [cartoonish gunshot] in the house!

98
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,502
You said "if something happens."

99
00:06:19,052 --> 00:06:20,178
It won't.

100
00:06:20,261 --> 00:06:22,639
[Nagisa] That pause implies it did.

101
00:06:24,015 --> 00:06:25,558
[sighs] Look,

102
00:06:25,642 --> 00:06:29,312
I acknowledge that I don't know
every last detail of the situation.

103
00:06:29,938 --> 00:06:33,691
But at least I wish you would've
told me about it sooner.

104
00:06:33,775 --> 00:06:35,318
For that, I'm sorry.

105
00:06:35,401 --> 00:06:37,070
- [grunts]
- No way!

106
00:06:37,946 --> 00:06:40,323
The match just started,
but the other guy's dominating.

107
00:06:42,117 --> 00:06:44,828
[sighs] Still... I don't get...

108
00:06:44,911 --> 00:06:48,081
how you could even consider
living with a stranger like that.

109
00:06:53,044 --> 00:06:56,339
Thing is, it's not like
Taiki was a total stranger.

110
00:06:57,006 --> 00:06:58,842
[both grunting]

111
00:06:58,925 --> 00:07:00,093
[Nishida] Ah, so close!

112
00:07:00,176 --> 00:07:01,636
He's keeping the rally going,

113
00:07:01,719 --> 00:07:03,596
but can't actually
take the point in the end.

114
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,932
It's totally meaningless
unless you can score.

115
00:07:06,015 --> 00:07:07,100
Haryu, come on.

116
00:07:07,183 --> 00:07:09,477
You could stand to be
a little nicer to Taiki.

117
00:07:09,561 --> 00:07:12,355
- Hey, we've seen you lose to him once!
- Come on!

118
00:07:13,606 --> 00:07:17,360
[Haryu] <i>This may be a practice match,
but if you don't step it up a notch,</i>

119
00:07:18,194 --> 00:07:20,613
<i>you're gonna get left behind again, Taiki.</i>

120
00:07:20,697 --> 00:07:23,324
[dramatic music playing]

121
00:07:24,701 --> 00:07:26,494
[panting]

122
00:07:33,543 --> 00:07:36,212
[Taiki] <i>I just casually decided
I wanted to go to nationals.</i>

123
00:07:36,296 --> 00:07:38,131
<i>And now I wanna punch myself for it.</i>

124
00:07:39,299 --> 00:07:42,510
<i>I have to be as good,
or even better than him.</i>

125
00:07:44,137 --> 00:07:48,850
<i>When I beat Haryu, I thought that meant
nationals were right around the corner.</i>

126
00:07:48,933 --> 00:07:52,353
<i>But in reality,
everybody else went to compete,</i>

127
00:07:52,437 --> 00:07:54,856
<i>and I watched from the sidelines.</i>

128
00:07:56,107 --> 00:07:57,442
<i>Then on top of that...</i>

129
00:08:00,862 --> 00:08:02,030
<i>I was flattered.</i>

130
00:08:02,655 --> 00:08:04,199
<i>Surprised, but flattered.</i>

131
00:08:04,866 --> 00:08:07,035
<i>Still, somewhere in my heart...</i>

132
00:08:08,995 --> 00:08:11,039
<i>I thought, "Me?"</i>

133
00:08:14,584 --> 00:08:15,585
[exhales]

134
00:08:16,628 --> 00:08:18,546
Hey, is he all right?

135
00:08:18,630 --> 00:08:20,048
Your housemate, I mean.

136
00:08:21,132 --> 00:08:23,092
His movements seem frantic.

137
00:08:23,176 --> 00:08:24,594
Doesn't he look desperate?

138
00:08:25,887 --> 00:08:26,804
[grunts]

139
00:08:27,764 --> 00:08:29,140
I'm sure that he's fine.

140
00:08:29,682 --> 00:08:31,059
He's just gotta move his legs.

141
00:08:33,895 --> 00:08:35,813
[Taiki] <i>And then there was that time...</i>

142
00:08:36,606 --> 00:08:37,941
From Chinatsu.

143
00:08:38,024 --> 00:08:39,567
They lost their game.

144
00:08:40,527 --> 00:08:42,445
[Taiki] <i>When Chinatsu was feeling low...</i>

145
00:08:42,529 --> 00:08:43,363
[grunts]

146
00:08:43,446 --> 00:08:44,864
You idiot! Not there!

147
00:08:46,449 --> 00:08:48,618
What the hell are you doing? Come on!

148
00:08:48,701 --> 00:08:50,620
This is where Yusa shines.

149
00:08:51,454 --> 00:08:53,373
He's running Taiki all over the court.

150
00:08:55,959 --> 00:08:58,878
[Taiki] <i>I was happy
I'm the one Chinatsu turned to.</i>

151
00:08:59,462 --> 00:09:00,880
<i>I wanted to cheer her up.</i>

152
00:09:01,464 --> 00:09:02,507
<i>But...</i>

153
00:09:11,057 --> 00:09:12,725
<i>Who do I think I am?</i>

154
00:09:15,186 --> 00:09:16,145
[grunts nervously]

155
00:09:17,230 --> 00:09:18,147
[grunts]

156
00:09:25,446 --> 00:09:26,573
[gasps]

157
00:09:28,449 --> 00:09:30,535
- You good?
- Yeah.

158
00:09:35,790 --> 00:09:36,833
[Yusa sighs]

159
00:09:39,711 --> 00:09:41,170
[game resumes]

160
00:09:41,879 --> 00:09:43,298
[both grunting]

161
00:09:48,928 --> 00:09:50,179
[pants]

162
00:09:53,391 --> 00:09:55,852
Badminton is a tough sport, huh?

163
00:09:56,394 --> 00:10:00,565
Keeping up with a birdie that moves
that fast has got to tire you out. Crazy.

164
00:10:00,648 --> 00:10:01,983
[grunts]

165
00:10:02,066 --> 00:10:03,818
[Hina] <i>The Taiki I know...</i>

166
00:10:04,569 --> 00:10:06,988
<i>has fun despite all the challenges.</i>

167
00:10:08,406 --> 00:10:09,657
[grunts]

168
00:10:10,158 --> 00:10:13,828
[Hina] <i>But this Taiki...
I've never seen this Taiki before.</i>

169
00:10:13,911 --> 00:10:16,331
[Taiki grunting]

170
00:10:17,206 --> 00:10:19,375
Argh, it's out! And all for nothing.

171
00:10:19,459 --> 00:10:21,127
That was his chance right there.

172
00:10:21,210 --> 00:10:24,589
At the end of a long rally,
missing can really screw with your head.

173
00:10:25,256 --> 00:10:28,217
And he was already worn out
after the first game.

174
00:10:28,301 --> 00:10:30,136
[panting]

175
00:10:42,231 --> 00:10:43,399
[exhales]

176
00:10:45,818 --> 00:10:49,530
[Chinatsu] <i>I'm starting to understand
what Taiki meant when he said...</i>

177
00:10:51,199 --> 00:10:56,371
[Taiki] <i>It's just me out on the court,
and I'm in control of the match's outcome.</i>

178
00:10:58,456 --> 00:10:59,624
<i>I know, Taiki.</i>

179
00:11:00,249 --> 00:11:03,503
<i>I know how hard you've worked
at morning practice every day.</i>

180
00:11:04,587 --> 00:11:09,008
<i>At first, I noticed there was some boy
who was always there.</i>

181
00:11:09,675 --> 00:11:13,012
<i>But it was literally every day.</i>

182
00:11:14,013 --> 00:11:15,640
<i>If he was there before me,</i>

183
00:11:15,723 --> 00:11:18,768
<i>I'd make it a competition
and come earlier the next day.</i>

184
00:11:22,021 --> 00:11:23,398
<i>You once said to me...</i>

185
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:26,192
[Taiki] <i>You were here practicing</i>

186
00:11:26,275 --> 00:11:28,986
<i>the day after you graduated
from your junior high club.</i>

187
00:11:31,572 --> 00:11:33,116
[Chinatsu] <i>But I saw you, too.</i>

188
00:11:34,325 --> 00:11:39,163
<i>I saw you practicing the very next day
after your final match of junior high.</i>

189
00:11:39,247 --> 00:11:40,164
[grunts]

190
00:11:40,248 --> 00:11:42,166
- Keep it up!
- You're doing good! Yeah!

191
00:11:42,250 --> 00:11:43,918
Nothing's getting past you!

192
00:11:44,001 --> 00:11:46,421
[both grunting]

193
00:11:46,504 --> 00:11:48,423
[inspirational music playing]

194
00:11:48,506 --> 00:11:50,174
[both panting]

195
00:11:53,010 --> 00:11:54,178
[Yusa] <i>It's uncanny.</i>

196
00:11:55,888 --> 00:11:58,182
<i>He's getting faster and faster.</i>

197
00:11:58,266 --> 00:11:59,684
[game resumes]

198
00:11:59,767 --> 00:12:01,185
[Chinatsu] <i>Even on rainy days,</i>

199
00:12:02,019 --> 00:12:03,062
<i>on windy days.</i>

200
00:12:03,771 --> 00:12:04,689
[grunts]

201
00:12:04,772 --> 00:12:06,691
- You got this, Taiki!
- Pedal to the metal!

202
00:12:08,776 --> 00:12:10,445
[both grunting]

203
00:12:13,781 --> 00:12:14,699
[all gasp]

204
00:12:15,533 --> 00:12:17,243
[Chinatsu] <i>No matter what the day brought,</i>

205
00:12:18,703 --> 00:12:20,746
<i>you never stopped moving forward.</i>

206
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:24,500
<i>I know that.</i>

207
00:12:25,293 --> 00:12:26,210
[grunts]

208
00:12:30,465 --> 00:12:31,674
[Yusa huffs]

209
00:12:32,550 --> 00:12:33,801
[pants]

210
00:12:40,933 --> 00:12:43,478
[Sajikawa player] Of course the final game
is a real nail-biter.

211
00:12:43,561 --> 00:12:46,731
It's like Yusa awakened
a sleeping beast from its slumber.

212
00:12:46,814 --> 00:12:48,983
This guy wasn't even on our radar before.

213
00:12:49,692 --> 00:12:53,488
<i>We've got a new rival standing in our way
of next year's nationals, and yet...</i>

214
00:12:54,238 --> 00:12:56,115
<i>it seems like he's having fun.</i>

215
00:12:57,575 --> 00:12:59,243
[both grunting]

216
00:13:01,579 --> 00:13:04,248
This rally is seriously intense, dude.

217
00:13:05,833 --> 00:13:09,003
Our man, Taiki,
he's returning every single shot...

218
00:13:09,629 --> 00:13:11,506
No, wait. He's actually starting to...

219
00:13:34,028 --> 00:13:36,405
Taiki just won the match!

220
00:13:36,489 --> 00:13:37,907
[all cheering]

221
00:13:39,033 --> 00:13:40,117
[boy 1] Nice work!

222
00:13:40,201 --> 00:13:41,327
[boy 2] You killed it!

223
00:13:42,495 --> 00:13:44,121
[panting]

224
00:13:53,256 --> 00:13:56,133
Incredible! Taiki did it! He won!

225
00:13:56,217 --> 00:13:58,678
'Kay. Back to rehearsal we go.

226
00:13:58,761 --> 00:13:59,595
What?

227
00:13:59,679 --> 00:14:02,223
You're okay with leaving
and not saying anything to him?

228
00:14:02,890 --> 00:14:04,892
Wait, what... Hina?

229
00:14:06,269 --> 00:14:07,812
Nice one, Taiki!

230
00:14:07,895 --> 00:14:10,398
To be honest, I didn't think
that you were gonna win, dude.

231
00:14:10,481 --> 00:14:11,816
But wow, what a match!

232
00:14:11,899 --> 00:14:14,193
To be honest, I didn't think
you were gonna win, dude.

233
00:14:14,277 --> 00:14:15,695
But your game's really come along.

234
00:14:15,778 --> 00:14:18,447
- Taiki. Your opponent.
- [Taiki] Right!

235
00:14:25,496 --> 00:14:26,706
Thank you for the match.

236
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:28,958
[Yusa] Hey.

237
00:14:29,625 --> 00:14:30,459
[Taiki gasps softly]

238
00:14:31,043 --> 00:14:32,044
I'm still...

239
00:14:32,545 --> 00:14:34,088
not satisfied yet.

240
00:14:37,216 --> 00:14:38,467
One more match then?

241
00:14:38,551 --> 00:14:39,594
Are you an idiot?

242
00:14:40,177 --> 00:14:43,347
You're obviously dead on your feet.
Yusa, you too.

243
00:14:43,931 --> 00:14:46,976
'Cause later,
you're gonna have to take me on.

244
00:14:59,030 --> 00:14:59,989
[laughs]

245
00:15:01,449 --> 00:15:03,117
I can't move anymore.

246
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,494
[inhales, exhales deeply]

247
00:15:07,121 --> 00:15:08,789
<i>I guess I am getting better.</i>

248
00:15:12,168 --> 00:15:13,836
[peaceful music playing]

249
00:15:23,512 --> 00:15:24,972
I just won!

250
00:15:26,641 --> 00:15:28,059
[grunts]

251
00:15:31,729 --> 00:15:33,814
[Chinatsu] You'll get sick
if you fall asleep there.

252
00:15:33,898 --> 00:15:34,732
[Taiki] Hm?

253
00:15:35,358 --> 00:15:36,525
Oh, Chinatsu!

254
00:15:38,861 --> 00:15:40,738
<i>That's right, she told me she'd come.</i>

255
00:15:41,364 --> 00:15:43,741
Left or right, you pick one.

256
00:15:43,824 --> 00:15:45,117
Huh?

257
00:15:45,201 --> 00:15:47,954
My treat. Choose left or right.

258
00:15:49,121 --> 00:15:51,499
- The right one.
- Right.

259
00:15:53,334 --> 00:15:54,835
[Taiki] Thank you very much.

260
00:15:54,919 --> 00:15:56,504
I was actually really thirsty.

261
00:15:58,756 --> 00:16:00,508
What was the left one, by the way?

262
00:16:00,591 --> 00:16:01,509
I'm holding it.

263
00:16:01,592 --> 00:16:03,427
So they were both the same!

264
00:16:03,970 --> 00:16:05,972
<i>There's that childlike side of her.</i>

265
00:16:06,681 --> 00:16:08,265
- No, they weren't.
- [exclaims]

266
00:16:08,349 --> 00:16:09,642
'Cause the right one

267
00:16:09,725 --> 00:16:12,770
was the one charged up
with my "high five" energy.

268
00:16:18,359 --> 00:16:20,653
[Taiki] <i>No wonder
I don't feel tired anymore.</i>

269
00:16:23,489 --> 00:16:27,118
Why is Pocari sweet
when you aren't exercising,

270
00:16:27,743 --> 00:16:30,538
but when you are exercising,
it doesn't taste as sweet?

271
00:16:31,664 --> 00:16:33,374
It's 'cause you're exhausted.

272
00:16:33,457 --> 00:16:35,918
Sure, I guess that's true, but...

273
00:16:36,002 --> 00:16:38,546
Also, you kinda sweated a lot.

274
00:16:38,629 --> 00:16:40,214
So you need to rehydrate.

275
00:16:40,798 --> 00:16:43,175
[sniffs] I must've looked dumb back there.

276
00:16:43,759 --> 00:16:45,177
No, you didn't look dumb.

277
00:16:46,512 --> 00:16:47,680
You looked pretty cool.

278
00:16:51,017 --> 00:16:52,309
That's nice of you.

279
00:16:53,185 --> 00:16:54,270
But today...

280
00:16:54,979 --> 00:16:57,148
my winning is really all thanks to you.

281
00:16:57,231 --> 00:16:58,065
[gasps]

282
00:16:58,733 --> 00:17:01,068
[Taiki] <i>You're at morning practice
every day,</i>

283
00:17:01,152 --> 00:17:03,571
<i>and then run miles and miles
at team practice.</i>

284
00:17:04,905 --> 00:17:07,575
<i>I think there are a lot of things
I've been able to do,</i>

285
00:17:07,658 --> 00:17:10,077
<i>just because
I've watched you work so hard.</i>

286
00:17:11,287 --> 00:17:13,831
So I will just
keep following your example.

287
00:17:14,665 --> 00:17:16,542
Today's match was still pretty close,

288
00:17:17,293 --> 00:17:18,836
but I'll score more next time.

289
00:17:19,837 --> 00:17:20,880
[grunts]

290
00:17:20,963 --> 00:17:23,966
[singing "Nagisa" by Spitz
from the distance]

291
00:17:24,050 --> 00:17:25,843
Oh, I know this song.

292
00:17:26,552 --> 00:17:29,221
They must be practicing
for the school festival.

293
00:17:29,305 --> 00:17:31,599
That's right.
It's just around the corner, huh?

294
00:17:31,682 --> 00:17:33,601
[Taiki] Wow, yeah, it almost fall.

295
00:17:33,684 --> 00:17:35,936
It's so much cooler now
than it was in August.

296
00:17:37,688 --> 00:17:39,356
[singing continues]

297
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:45,404
[singing "Nagisa" by Spitz]

298
00:17:59,710 --> 00:18:02,922
[In English] I thought, for some reason,
you'd be good at singing.

299
00:18:03,005 --> 00:18:04,632
- [exclaims] Hey!
- [laughs]

300
00:18:04,715 --> 00:18:06,634
Did you need to say that out loud?

301
00:18:06,717 --> 00:18:08,135
Okay. I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

302
00:18:09,512 --> 00:18:12,890
<i>I said it 'cause I was happy
to see a new side of her.</i>

303
00:18:13,599 --> 00:18:15,392
Are you good at singing, Taiki?

304
00:18:15,476 --> 00:18:17,228
Nah, just average.

305
00:18:17,311 --> 00:18:19,188
Why do I not believe you at all?

306
00:18:19,271 --> 00:18:20,773
No, really.

307
00:18:21,607 --> 00:18:23,776
Hina's actually a pretty good singer.

308
00:18:24,401 --> 00:18:25,945
She gives off that vibe.

309
00:18:26,487 --> 00:18:29,532
And speaking of...
Hina came to watch your match, too.

310
00:18:29,615 --> 00:18:32,827
Oh, right.
She had a break from rehearsing the...

311
00:18:34,078 --> 00:18:35,663
[Hina] <i>Wanna do it for real?</i>

312
00:18:36,539 --> 00:18:37,414
...play.

313
00:18:37,498 --> 00:18:39,166
Ah, whatever,

314
00:18:39,250 --> 00:18:41,669
you could say I won
'cause of everyone's support, right?

315
00:18:42,503 --> 00:18:43,838
<i>I gotta chill out.</i>

316
00:18:43,921 --> 00:18:46,215
<i>It's not like the two of us
actually did it.</i>

317
00:18:46,882 --> 00:18:48,551
- Is the play going well?
- [gasps]

318
00:18:49,135 --> 00:18:51,929
I saw folks making set pieces
in the courtyard.

319
00:18:52,012 --> 00:18:55,266
Yeah, so far.
It's moving along for the most part.

320
00:18:55,349 --> 00:18:57,101
Yeah? That's great!

321
00:18:57,184 --> 00:18:58,185
I'll be there.

322
00:18:58,769 --> 00:18:59,812
Sounds good!

323
00:18:59,895 --> 00:19:02,189
The adaptation is unique,
so it should be fun.

324
00:19:03,107 --> 00:19:05,818
- And the kiss?
- It definitely didn't happen!

325
00:19:05,901 --> 00:19:06,777
Huh?

326
00:19:07,278 --> 00:19:08,821
[groans]

327
00:19:09,446 --> 00:19:12,241
I was just wondering
how your class will handle it in the play.

328
00:19:12,324 --> 00:19:14,785
Uh, they are... they're just gonna fake it.

329
00:19:15,327 --> 00:19:18,038
[Nishida] Huh? Taiki! Where are you?

330
00:19:18,873 --> 00:19:21,584
- Well that's my cue. Bye!
- Bye.

331
00:19:30,634 --> 00:19:32,428
[Coach Yuasa]
Thank you for everything today.

332
00:19:32,511 --> 00:19:33,846
[Sajikawa coach] Same to you.

333
00:19:34,471 --> 00:19:36,640
- [boy 1] We're heading out.
- [boy 2] This way, c'mon.

334
00:19:37,808 --> 00:19:39,351
- [Taiki] Yusa.
- Hm?

335
00:19:40,019 --> 00:19:41,020
You left this.

336
00:19:41,604 --> 00:19:42,938
It's yours, isn't it?

337
00:19:43,022 --> 00:19:44,607
Oh. Thank you.

338
00:19:44,690 --> 00:19:45,524
Sure.

339
00:19:45,608 --> 00:19:46,567
[boy] Inomata!

340
00:19:47,735 --> 00:19:49,361
- See ya.
- Inomata.

341
00:19:50,988 --> 00:19:51,864
What's up?

342
00:19:51,947 --> 00:19:53,115
Your name...

343
00:19:54,158 --> 00:19:56,619
Is it the kanji for "wild boar"
and "hip joint?"

344
00:19:57,244 --> 00:19:58,996
Well, you're not wrong.

345
00:19:59,079 --> 00:20:00,664
I can't remember anyone's names

346
00:20:00,748 --> 00:20:03,375
unless I learn what characters
they write them with.

347
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:05,461
So, later,

348
00:20:06,003 --> 00:20:06,962
Inomata.

349
00:20:08,756 --> 00:20:10,633
Yeah, later.

350
00:20:12,384 --> 00:20:14,428
<i>It'll be a real match next time.</i>

351
00:20:17,973 --> 00:20:19,975
Hey, Haryu, wanna switch--

352
00:20:20,059 --> 00:20:21,727
- Better to leave him.
- Huh?

353
00:20:21,810 --> 00:20:22,895
Wait, why, though?

354
00:20:23,687 --> 00:20:27,942
[Nishida] Because he just lost to Yusa.
I don't recommend poking that bear.

355
00:20:32,446 --> 00:20:34,323
[Yukiko] Taiki! Dinner is ready!

356
00:20:35,241 --> 00:20:36,367
Taiki!

357
00:20:36,909 --> 00:20:38,077
[Dad] He must be asleep.

358
00:20:39,286 --> 00:20:41,163
His food will get cold, though.

359
00:20:41,247 --> 00:20:43,165
Aw, let the kid catch some Z's honey.

360
00:20:43,249 --> 00:20:45,542
Didn't he have a practice match today?

361
00:20:45,626 --> 00:20:47,753
- [snoring]
- [Dad] He looked pretty worn out.

362
00:20:53,384 --> 00:20:55,511
[announcer]
<i>It's the final match of the qualifiers!</i>

363
00:20:55,594 --> 00:20:57,137
<i>And what a heated match it is!</i>

364
00:20:57,221 --> 00:20:59,223
<i>An intense rally continues...</i>

365
00:20:59,306 --> 00:21:01,225
<i>- And Inomata scores the final point!</i>
- [yells]

366
00:21:01,308 --> 00:21:05,312
[announcer] <i>Taiki Inomata from
Eimei Private High School is the champion!</i>

367
00:21:05,938 --> 00:21:07,523
I lost, Inomata.

368
00:21:08,148 --> 00:21:09,566
You destroyed me.

369
00:21:11,193 --> 00:21:12,027
Rematch?

370
00:21:12,778 --> 00:21:14,655
- How 'bout right now?
- Huh?

371
00:21:15,155 --> 00:21:16,073
[Chinatsu] Taiki.

372
00:21:16,156 --> 00:21:17,199
[grunts]

373
00:21:17,283 --> 00:21:18,325
Hi, Chinatsu.

374
00:21:19,285 --> 00:21:20,619
You were watching me?

375
00:21:20,703 --> 00:21:23,330
Mm-hm. Congratulations, champion.

376
00:21:24,081 --> 00:21:25,457
You looked great out there.

377
00:21:26,166 --> 00:21:27,334
Thank you very much.

378
00:21:27,918 --> 00:21:30,671
And now, a congratulation smooch.

379
00:21:30,754 --> 00:21:31,714
What?

380
00:21:31,797 --> 00:21:33,465
Wait...

381
00:21:34,133 --> 00:21:35,175
Oh, no.

382
00:21:36,552 --> 00:21:38,637
Chinatsu.

383
00:21:40,556 --> 00:21:41,849
TUG

384
00:21:42,808 --> 00:21:44,351
Oh, no, not on my watch.

385
00:21:44,435 --> 00:21:45,728
Hina?

386
00:21:47,104 --> 00:21:47,938
Uh...

387
00:21:49,315 --> 00:21:50,983
[screams]

388
00:22:01,869 --> 00:22:03,787
<i>What kind of dream was that!</i>

389
00:22:05,622 --> 00:22:07,624
[closing theme song playing]
